      "writtenOn": "2018-09-19T08:37:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This could delay the fallback probe by 3s for users that do not need a fallback HTTPS URL. I think that you could instead do the same thing that is done with the main HTTPS and HTTP URL, using the fallback HTTPS and HTTP URLs (sending the probes in parallel, factoring out code to reuse it in both cases).\n\nWith this change it\u0027s possible that captive portals that have https://*.gstatic.com whitelisted (through SNI) won\u0027t be detected anymore and will break.\nOne future improvement we have considered is to unvalidate a network if the HTTPS probe went through first (and the network was validated), but the HTTP probe returned shortly after and saw a portal. Reusing the same code for the main HTTP/HTTPS and fallback HTTP/HTTPS checks could allow us to also easily implement that same logic for the fallback HTTP/HTTPS checks, and resolve the above issue where https://*.gstatic.com is whitelisted.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1239,
        "startChar": 25,
        "endLine": 1239,
        "endChar": 30
      },
